# No d3d9 flag: Gallium Nine is gone from mesa. media-libs/mesa-26.0.8 has no
# `d3d9` and no `nine` anywhere in the ebuild, so the flag named a state mesa can
# no longer be in -- and Portage ignores an unknown package.use flag in silence
# (checked 2026-09-08).
media-libs/mesa lm-sensors opencl
media-libs/libvpx postproc
# No libdrm[video_cards_radeon]. That flag builds libdrm_radeon, which serves
# mesa's r300/r600 gallium drivers -- and package.use/00video_cards clears
# VIDEO_CARDS with "-*" and does not list `radeon`, so mesa builds neither.
# radeonsi uses the amdgpu winsys, not this one. The line was building a library
# with no consumer in the plan.
#
# TRADE-OFF: pre-GCN AMD cards (HD 2000-6000) fall back to llvmpipe on the live
# ISO. Adding `radeon` to VIDEO_CARDS is the fix if that matters -- this line
# alone would not have helped, since mesa is what needs the flag (2026-09-09).
media-libs/vulkan-loader layers
